{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause (AC1), read from the full log of sweep job 133312625052 (run 43871224211, 2026-11-16):\n\n1. 19 tests, `Error while loading plugin \"pytest11\"`. Every child traceback shows the same chain: anyio/pytest_plugin.py:309 `get_available_backends()` imports `anyio._backends._asyncio`, which imports `asyncio`, which imports `windows_events`, which imports `_overlapped`. That import fails with `OSError: [WinError 10106] The requested service provider could not be loaded or initialized` (92 occurrences in the log). Each of the 19 tests passes `run_nested_pytest` a minimal env, for example `{sentinel, guarded var, PATH}` at test_environ_assert_repr_security.py:136, so the child has no `SYSTEMROOT`. Winsock cannot initialize without it.\n2. 8 tests, `AssertionError: root conftest plugin not registered`, raised by `_root_conftest` (test_repo_isolation_guard.py:435-445). Its check `name.endswith(\"tests/conftest.py\")` never matches on Windows, where pytest registers the conftest under its native path `D:\\a\\rebar\\rebar\\tests\\conftest.py`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795069292515771605,"uuid":"c2309ba5-19ca-49e3-b825-96927d7247a4"}